                        "review": "I went in knowing it is like half the game and even not the romance heavy one. It started really slow and kinda boring a lot but it grew on me. I wouldn't say it's a good romance though. It's very vague and often you have no idea which choices lead do whom which is a bit ridiculous. \n\nBut the story, the politics, the stuff happening and the pressure\\angst slightly creeping in make it just an interesting visial novel to read (which I am usually not a fan of). The hardest are first couple of hours when the plot does not plotting and the protaginist just sits in her room all the time with nothing to happen. The controls for the PC are cluncky but doable, but the visuals will always be hardcoded controller so I have to google which key does what (I am not whipping out my controller just to press \"next\") dozens of times.\n\nI have finished the game and moving on to the Blossom, but honestly... I did not expect it to be that heartwrenching. It starts silly and then creeps, creeps up on you and then you're sad, and worried. It made me feel things, mostly nothing to do with romance. OST is beaituful. I feel like I need something happy and stupid after I finish the second part. I can't leave it but yeah, the shit is real. Or maybe I am too much of a feely girly. So much hopelessnes. \n\nI only wish they'd make the protagonist less of a placeholder that's basically a useless rag with basically no voice or impact of her own. She just walks around occasionally screaming. She doesn't deserve any of the guys, lol.",
